  "title": "The division of Sunni and Shia Islam",
  "summary": "Sunni and Shia identities first formed around a dispute over who should lead the Muslim community after Muhammad's death in 632. The First Fitna (656–661), a civil war between Caliph Ali and Muawiya, governor of Syria, saw Ali move his capital to Kufa; he was assassinated in 661. Over time the political divide broadened to include theological differences and differences in practice. Sunni and Shia remain the two main sects of Islam.",
